Subject: [PATCH] omap_hsmmc: PBIAS settle + gate DMAE to data commands (B4 MMC throughput)

On the early BeagleBoard (Rev A-B4) the OMAP3 HSMMC negotiates a clean
25 MHz / 4-bit high-speed link but delivers only ~0.6 MB/s read and ~0.1 MB/s
write, with NO CRC/timeout errors logged. Root cause: the DMA-enable (DMAE)
command bit was set on *every* command, including the non-data status polls
(CMD13) the driver issues between blocks, so each such command stalls waiting
on a DMA transfer that never runs. Writes are hit hardest because they busy-poll
the card (CMD13) after every block. Gate DMAE to commands that actually carry a
data phase. Also add a 20 ms PBIAS/rail settle after power-on for this marginal
board.

This is the same fix as the recovery kernel's patch 0002 (Linux 6.6), ported
for the OpenPVRSGX 7.2 Devuan kernel. Driver-only -- independent of the DTB, so
it applies whichever omap3-beagle DTB is used. Applied with `patch -p1 -l
--fuzz=3` (line offsets differ from 6.6; the anchor code is unchanged).
---
 drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/omap_hsmmc.c
@@ -344,6 +344,8 @@ static int omap_hsmmc_set_power(struct omap_hsmmc_host *host, int power_on)
 		ret = omap_hsmmc_set_pbias(host, true);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_set_voltage;
+
+		msleep(20); /* PBIAS/rail settle for marginal OMAP3 board */
 	} else {
 		ret = omap_hsmmc_disable_supply(mmc);
 		if (ret)
@@ -798,7 +800,7 @@ omap_hsmmc_start_command(struct omap_hsmmc_host *host, struct mmc_command *cmd,
 			cmdreg &= ~(DDIR);
 	}
 
-	if (host->use_dma)
+	if (host->use_dma && data)
 		cmdreg |= DMAE;
 
 	host->req_in_progress = 1;
